1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--monologuing","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/monologuing","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/monologuing","sourceHash":"2bcb341e20aff8a9bea3eeea60488f279f8be9218edcfabf68131fabc617533f","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:53:25.943Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Monologuing","zh":"独白练习"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Monologuing means speaking by yourself in the target language — narrating your day, describing what you see, reacting to something, or just talking about whatever comes to mind. No conversation partner needed.","zh":"独白练习是指独自用目标语言说话——讲述自己的一天、描述看到的事物、对某件事作出反应，或只是想到什么就说什么。不需要对话伙伴。"}},{"id":"why-it-helps","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It Helps","zh":"为什么有帮助"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Monologuing lets you practice word retrieval and sentence construction without the pressure of a listener. You can pause, restart, and try different phrasings without social awkwardness. It's the speaking equivalent of freewriting.","zh":"独白练习让你能在没有听众压力的情况下，练习提取词汇和组织句子。你可以停顿、重新开始并尝试不同说法，不必担心社交上的尴尬。它相当于口语版的自由写作。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"It's also always available. You don't need to schedule a partner, pay for a tutor, or have internet access. You can monologue while walking, cooking, driving, or any time you're alone. Or when you're with people, I guess... But that'd be a little weird.","zh":"而且你随时都可以练习。无需与伙伴约时间、花钱请老师或连接互联网。你可以在走路、做饭、开车时，或任何独处的时候练习独白。当然，和别人在一起时似乎也行……不过那样会有点奇怪。"}},{"id":"methods","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Methods","zh":"练习方法"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Narration:</strong> Describe what you're doing in real-time (\"I'm walking to the store, it's cold outside...\")","zh":"<strong>实时叙述：</strong> 实时描述自己正在做的事（“我正走去商店，外面很冷……”）"},{"en":"<strong>Vlogging:</strong> Record yourself talking to a camera for 5-10 minutes. You don't need to publish it (but if you do, share with us! We love to see people using their language)","zh":"<strong>视频日志：</strong> 对着镜头录制一段 5 到 10 分钟的讲话。你不必发布它（但如果发布了，请分享给我们！我们很喜欢看到大家使用自己所学的语言）"},{"en":"<strong>Reacting:</strong> Watch a video or read something, then talk about it out loud","zh":"<strong>发表感想：</strong> 看一段视频或读一些内容，然后大声谈谈自己的看法"},{"en":"<strong>Thinking out loud:</strong> Express your thoughts and opinions on anything","zh":"<strong>自言自语：</strong> 表达你对任何事情的想法和观点"}]},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"技巧"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Don't worry about mistakes — the goal is to keep talking","zh":"不用担心犯错——目标是持续说下去"},{"en":"If you get stuck on a word, describe the concept differently instead of switching to your native language","zh":"如果被某个词卡住了，就换一种方式描述这个概念，而不要切换成母语"},{"en":"Recording yourself is optional but useful for later Speaking Analysis","zh":"录下自己的讲话并非必需，但有助于之后进行口语分析"},{"en":"This is the easiest method for getting a large number of speaking hours without breaking the bank!","zh":"这是不用花费太多钱就能积累大量口语练习时数的最简单方法！"}]},{"id":"when-to-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Start","zh":"何时开始"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Monologuing is introduced in Phase 4A and remains useful throughout all later phases.","zh":"独白练习会在阶段 4A 引入，并在之后的所有阶段持续发挥作用。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
